  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2017 Humanitarian Response for Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing conflict and subsequent deep humanitarian crisis in eastern Ukraine continues to increase the vulnerability of households remaining in both the government controlled areas (GCA) and non-government controlled areas (NGCA). Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to addressing the humanitarian and early recovery needs of the most vulnerable persons affected by conflict in eastern Ukraine through: 1. Distribution of coal and cast-iron stoves for the most vulnerable households to meet their heating needs for the upcoming winter; 2. Shelter and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) rehabilitations in social institutions and key community sites; and 3. Pilot livelihood support in the selected areas witnessing a major flow of returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
